olio.in/services/full-stack-development/#service\",\"name\":\"Full Stack Development Services\",\"serviceType\":\"Full Stack Development\",\"description\":\"Hire a full stack developer for end-to-end product builds: React and Next.js frontends, Python FastAPI backends, PostgreSQL, Docker, and AWS deployment.\",\"url\":\"https://pavansharmaportfolio.in/services/full-stack-development/\",\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https://pavansharmaportfolio.in/#person\",\"name\":\"Pavan Sharma\"},\"areaServed\":[\"United States\",\"United Kingdom\",\"Canada\",\"Australia\",\"Europe\",\"United Arab Emirates\",\"Worldwide\"],\"availableChannel\":{\"@type\":\"ServiceChannel\",\"serviceUrl\":\"https://pavansharmaportfolio.in/contact/\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What stack do you use for full stack projects?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"React or Next.js with TypeScript and Tailwind on the frontend; Python FastAPI on the backend; PostgreSQL or MongoDB for data; Docker for packaging; AWS (EC2, S3, Lambda) for hosting. I pick the simplest architecture that serves the product.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can you take over an existing codebase?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. I start with a code audit, stabilize the riskiest parts, and then ship improvements incrementally — no big-bang rewrites unless the code genuinely demands it.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do you also handle deployment and DevOps?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes — Dockerized builds, AWS deployment, domains/SSL, monitoring basics, and documentation. My CloudOps project is exactly this discipline turned into a product.\"}}]}"}}],"$L18"]]}]]}],"$L19"]}]
